    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193193_492702_23766" xmi:uuid="da113b90-9de6-4908-bbe7-679ffbe3ef35" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455124019197_747389_42321" xmi:uuid="0a66f26a-0c4c-4112-84c5-a94fbe02f2ca" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193193_492702_23766"/>
        <body> A ProcessPlanRelationship is an association between two ProcessPlan objects. &lt;example&gt;If a part shall be manufactured in two different manufacturing sites, such as one in Paris and the other in Bordeaux, there will be two different process plans, that may be related by a ProcessPlanRelationship.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ProcessPlanRelationship</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459331077251_874034_42685" xmi:uuid="d6bc036e-83e8-4550-93cb-48496b16d49e" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459331111289_25857_42687" xmi:uuid="3ccc16a6-685a-46bb-8b2a-4b20caa84c71" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459331077251_874034_42685"/>
          <body>the related ProcessPlan and the relating ProcessPlan shall be different.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671209121873_702620_163150" xmi:uuid="554a092f-2678-4344-8970-b751124c9d87" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671209121873_264953_163151" xmi:uuid="1538f91d-0f68-43a2-bb11-f88f3b92c938" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>WR1: Relating :&lt;&gt;: Related;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>EXPRESS</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671209121873_161358_163148" xmi:uuid="fe59ec35-f9e9-4b61-9500-fdd762b52637" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671209121873_254544_163149" xmi:uuid="129c0558-6b21-4fcb-ae1d-89edd1b3bc98" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//ProcessPlanRelationship[@uid]"&gt;&#13; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt;&#13; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt;&#13; &lt;sch:let name="uidRelating" value="../@uid"/&gt;&#13; &lt;sch:let name="uidRelated" value="Related/@uidRef"/&gt;&#13; &lt;sch:assert test="not(../@uid = Related/@uidRef)"&gt;&#13; The related ProcessPlan and the relating ProcessPlan shall be different. &#13; {&#13; -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt;&#13; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; &#13; -rule_name:ProcessPlanRelationship.WR1&#13; -relating:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uidRelating"/&gt;&#13; -related:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uidRelated"/&gt;&#13; }&#13; &lt;/sch:assert&gt;&#13; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193193_492702_23766"/>
